title: 'pallet-validator-collators: drop validators that author no blocks'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-validator-collators` can stop returning, for a number of Aura slots, validators that
    miss a number of their Aura turns in a row. Governance sets the rule with the new
    `set_drop_rule` call. Without a rule, the default, nobody is dropped. The pallet reads the
    slot of each block from the Aura pre-runtime digest, counts each empty slot as a missed turn
    of the authority it belongs to, and adds these turns to the validators at each session
    rotation. A gap longer than the authority list counts no missed turn. New storage items:
    `CountedSlots`, `MissedTurns`, `CurrentDropRule`, `LastActivity` and `Dropped`. No migration.

    `pallet_validator_collators::Config` now requires `pallet_session::Config` with
    `ValidatorId = AccountId`: the pallet reads the session validators, the Aura authorities in
    the same order. It gains `MaxTrackedAuthorities`, the bound of `MissedTurns`, which Asset Hub
    Westend and People Westend wire.
crates:
- name: pallet-validator-collators
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-validator-set-announcer
  bump: none
- name: people-westend-integration-tests
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-zombienet-sdk-tests
  bump: none
